# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vendor-probes-artifact-upload-bloat -- vendor:probes:* uploads 39701 files and hangs the CAD runner retrying
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: ci-infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-27

* Symptom

vendor:probes:bricscad (job 17509199185, PF5S26B, MR !497's pipeline): the
probes ran and passed in a few minutes (entity-lifecycle 97 conforms / 4
known divergences / 0 unexpected; drawing-data, selection PASS), then:

: dist/vendor-probes/: found 39701 matching artifact files and directories
: ERROR: Uploading artifacts as "archive" to coordinator... error ... invalid argument
: WARNING: Retrying...

for more than 25 minutes, holding the single CAD runner (the AutoCAD job
queued behind it). Cancelled by hand.

* Likely cause

PROBE_KEEP_WORKDIR=1: each probe's workdir is copied into
dist/vendor-probes/<backend>/<probe>-workdir. dist/ is untracked and the
Windows runner reuses its build directory, so if the copies (or the
workdirs they come from) are never cleaned, they accumulate run after run;
39701 entries is far beyond one run's four workdirs.

* To do

1. On the runner: count what dist/vendor-probes/ holds and where it comes
   from (one run's copies, or every run's).
2. Clean dist/vendor-probes/ at the start of the job (or copy only the
   protocol/ and log files a reader needs, not whole workdirs).
3. Bound the artifact (paths / exclude), so a bad run fails fast instead of
   retrying an upload for half an hour on the CAD runner.
